==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed Giraffe Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed Lion Cat''' after obtaining from [[Ruthless Tyrant (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Brainwashed Cow Cat can be used in the same way as his [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|other]] [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|variants]], due to having a similar amount of spammability and stats midway between them.

His unique asset is the ability to permanently Curse anything he's attacking (assuming it's the right trait), for as long as he sticks to them, which gives him some extra use against a couple of enemies. Sadly, even that may be an overstatement. When it comes to Dark enemies, he could give certain tanky units some chances to avoid [[Masked Okame|Okame]]'s knockback, or it could hold [[Samurai Doggy]] in place alongside a tank, but that is pretty much it, as few Darks have abilities and many who do counter this unit in various ways. Against the Aku, he would find more matches, especially with [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] due to its minimal shield defense, but he's otherwise hindered by Shields stopping abilities from working, thus rarely making it worth using for this ability, even with sufficient shield pierces.

Outside of this usage, he's outclassed by [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]] the moment you acquire it. It can still be used before then, however, such as in Empire of Cats.

=== '''True Form''' ===
This True Form adds little to the unit, reducing its knockback count and increasing its curse duration. The lower knockback count does allow it to curse threats easily and the extra curse duration improves its uptime a bit if enemies manage to ward it off. Unfortunately, these improvements are completely irrelevant due to it retaining its poor niche.

